# =============================================================================
# .github/CODEOWNERS
# =============================================================================
# Defines required reviewers for sensitive paths.
#
# SEC_INTENT: gate script, fixture, and workflow changes require an explicit
# human review. The agent-loop (auto-fix) is explicitly EXCLUDED from owning
# these paths — it runs as a bot account (floci-agent-loop) and can never
# approve its own PRs.
#
# Coverage:
#   *              → default reviewer for any unmatched path
#   terraform/     → infra changes reviewed by security lead (covers both
#                    modules/security/ and modules/azure-security/ already,
#                    listed separately below for emphasis)
#   scripts/scan.sh, toggle-fixture.sh, toggle-fixture-azure.sh → gate
#                    integrity — requires review
#   .github/       → workflow changes — prevents privilege escalation
#   modules/security/, modules/azure-security/ → misconfig fixtures live
#                    here (AVD-AWS-0057, AVD-AZU-0013) — requires review
# =============================================================================

# Default: all files need review
*                                     @arifbazli

# Terraform infra
/terraform/                           @arifbazli

# Security module (contains the deliberate misconfig fixture)
/terraform/modules/security/          @arifbazli

# Azure security module (contains the deliberate misconfig fixture — AVD-AZU-0013)
/terraform/modules/azure-security/    @arifbazli

# Gate scripts — any change here must be manually reviewed
/scripts/scan.sh                      @arifbazli
/scripts/toggle-fixture.sh            @arifbazli
/scripts/toggle-fixture-azure.sh      @arifbazli
/scripts/deploy.sh                    @arifbazli
/scripts/agent-loop.sh                @arifbazli

# AI triage (agent allowlist)
/scripts/ai/                          @arifbazli

# Workflow definitions — prevent privilege escalation via workflow edits
/.github/                             @arifbazli
